From 64e8d7c70ba4c6d4e87ae49b7be9703a7ea2866e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:42:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.5: Policy Routing Rung B, speed-test instrumentation,
 diag v1.3.13, Warden resolver carve-out

Policy Routing commit-confirm (Rung B, F6-F11): the page polls the whole confirm
window instead of 8.4 s; the duplicate ipset rebuild per apply is gone
(PBR_SETS_DONE); Keep/Revert acknowledge their responses on both pages; the
deadline is stamped after the work; the revert runs under the firewall lock,
checks its result and reports REVERT FAILED; the arm token is taken first so
confirm and revert cannot race; confirm reports an incomplete save; error
codes (E_*) replace prose and the page translates them; runtime keys get
router_defaults entries.

/tmp/resolv.dnsmasq is dnsmasq's servers-file (server= lines): the Warden
self-filter resolver carve-out and reaper_diag section 5 both parsed it for
nameserver lines and matched nothing. Both fixed.

Internet speed test (10 Gbit/s field reports): every engine launch goes
through /usr/sbin/ookla_run (stderr kept per run, nice -10, argv untouched);
the page names the failure (timeout / engine error with the engine's message /
launch failed / WAN down); reaper_diag 10b reports the host-TCP offload state,
RT throttling, and the last run's messages.

reaper_diag v1.3.13: socket ceilings, QoS cap finding, rmcpd shown as arm-gated,
resolver derivation fixed. Speed-test page shows the QoS cap. Long translations
clip to one line with a hover tooltip on every new message surface. 17 new
dict tokens x 25 languages, lockstep 6820.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
